{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And to dust you shall return.</b> The intent concerns the mystical secret of the verse that Elihu mentioned regarding the repentance of the men of iniquity, and the discerning will understand. And this is what they say in the Midrash: ״ואל עפר תשוב״ — 'you shall return' — it is not written here תבא but תשוב; from this is an allusion to the revival of the dead, for He had already mentioned ״עד שובך״. And it is possible to say that ״ואל עפר תשוב״ alludes to that which he is destined to say: ״ואנכי עפר ואפר״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:53.005704326Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}